  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nThe lathe stock sim cuts groove/part and form tools (and axial, meridian thread passes) with their true blade profile instead of refusing them (`LATHE_BLADE_REFUSAL` is gone). A helical program - the Threading op's half-turn passes - is refused by name at plan time (`LATHE_THREAD_REFUSAL`; any other tool arcing about the spindle: `LATHE_HELIX_REFUSAL`), never revolved into rings of cut crests.\r\n\r\n- New `stock_sim/field_blade.rs`, `LatheProfile`:\r\n  - **Nose:** inserts and boring bars, unchanged.\r\n  - **Blade:** a rectangle of `width` with `corner_r` corners.\r\n  - **Thread:** a V at `tip_angle`, truncated at `width` (the crest).\r\n  - **Form:** the crown arc of `nose_radius` across `width`, as straight segments with ends on the arc, under-reading by at most 1e-4 mm and never over-cutting. A form band wider than its crown, or a NaN/oversize blade corner, refuses by name at plan time (no clamp, no rectangle stand-in).\r\n- The same reading as #103's rapid law: the tip sits at the centre of the width and the body extends outward. Body height is the tool's `flute_len` (the field is finite).\r\n- An exact swept distance per move; a part-off past the centre is handled.\r\n- New `Stock::simulate_lathe_profile`; `simulate_lathe`/`_about` call it with the nose shape. Entry points moved to `field_lathe.rs` (`backend.rs` 455 â†’ 410).\r\n- App: `LathePlan` carries the profile from the tool; a blade's display cell is sized from half its width. The column verdict still refuses lathe programs by name.\r\n\r\n## Pins\r\n\r\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/21-blade-sweep.md`.\r\n- `crates/sim/tests/stock_lathe_blade.rs` (5): every cell is checked against a fine-stamped true profile. Plunge groove with corner, part-off past centre, two-pass 60Â° thread and form sink each have **0 under-cut, 0 beyond resolution** (13kâ€“22k cells each). Nonsense profiles are refused by name.\r\n- `lathe_field_tools::a_generated_threading_op_refuses_the_field_by_name`: a generated Threading op through `field_view_with` gets the named thread refusal, not the \"skewed chord\" error (fails without the gate).\r\n- `lathe_field_tools::a_generated_form_op_cuts_its_crown_on_the_field`: a generated FormTurning op cuts its valley at every azimuth and leaves steel beside and under it.\r\n- `lathe_field_sim::a_grooving_blade_cuts_its_rectangle_and_the_verdict_refuses_the_lathe` replaces the old refusal test: 0 sign misses over 439k cells.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\n- **sim:** lib and all stock suites green.\r\n- **app:** lathe_field_sim, lathe_field_tools, every turning_* suite, and the stock_*/sim suites green after merging main (75d1b30).\r\n- **Clippy:** clean on sim and app.\r\n- **Goldens:** none changed.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The lathe stock sim cuts grooving/parting and form tools with their true blade profile (rectangle with corner radii, form crown) instead of refusing them; helical threading passes are still refused by name\r\n\r\nFixes #21\r\n\r\nðŸ¤– Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n",
